---
import Article from "../../layouts/Article.astro";
import Leaderboard from "../../components/Leaderboard.astro";
import TierPicks from "../../components/TierPicks.astro";
import { data, ranked, monthYear, fmtDate, solvedBy, codingTotal, nCodingTasks } from "../../lib/data";
import { rankingPosts, shortDate } from "../../lib/posts";

const post = rankingPosts()[1];
const rows = ranked("coding");
const nTasks = nCodingTasks();
const when = monthYear();
const title = `Best Local LLM for Coding (${when}): We Ran the Code`;
const description = `Which AI model you can run on your own computer writes code that actually works? We gave ${rows.length} models the same ${nTasks} programming jobs and ran their code. Updated ${fmtDate(data.generated)}.`;
const top = rows[0];
const ties = rows.filter((m) => m.suites.coding?.score === top.suites.coding?.score);
const toc = [
  { href: "#gpu", label: "Pick by graphics card" },
  { href: "#mac", label: "Pick by Mac" },
  { href: "#leaderboard", label: "All models, ranked by coding" },
  { href: "#limits", label: "What this test doesn't cover" },
];
---
<Article
  seoTitle={title}
  description={description}
  heading={`Best local LLM for coding: ${when}`}
  dek={`We gave ${rows.length} local models the same ${nTasks} small programming jobs, then ran their code against tests they never saw. A job only counts if the code works completely.`}
  kicker={`Rankings · updated ${shortDate(data.generated)}`}
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { href: "/topics/coding/", label: "Coding" }]}
  cover={post.cover}
  toc={toc}
  nav="rankings"
>
  <div class="short">
    <strong>The short version</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The best coders solved {solvedBy(top)} of {codingTotal(top)} jobs:
        {ties.slice(0, 4).map((m, i) => <>{i > 0 && ", "}<a href={`/models/${m.slug}/`} style="color: var(--blue)">{m.name}</a></>)}{ties.length > 4 && ` and ${ties.length - 4} more`}.
      </li>
      <li>The jobs are things like reading dates, cleaning up messy data and building a simple stock tracker.</li>
      <li>Below: the best coder that fits each graphics card and Mac.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="prose"><h2 id="gpu">Pick by graphics card</h2></div>
  <TierPicks by="coding" kind="gpu" />
  <div class="prose"><h2 id="mac">Pick by Mac</h2></div>
  <TierPicks by="coding" kind="mac" />
  <div class="prose" style="max-width: none"><h2 id="leaderboard">All models, ranked by coding</h2></div>
  <Leaderboard by="coding" />

  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="limits">What this test doesn't cover</h2>
    <p>
      These are short jobs that fit in one file, the kind of thing you'd ask a chatbot for. We don't test big projects spread over many
      files, and we don't measure how fast a model runs on your machine. You can see five of the jobs, and every model's answer, on each
      model's review page. <a href="/best-local-llms/methodology/">Full technical details</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div slot="tags" class="chips"><a class="chip" href="/topics/coding/">Coding</a><a class="chip" href="/topics/rankings/">Rankings</a></div>
</Article>
